        <mxCell id="regression-159" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;\(\bar{x}=\frac{1}{n}\sum x_i\) (mean) — the line always passes through \((\bar{x},\bar{y})\)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Works only for small problems; with many features use the Normal Equation \(\beta=(X^TX)^{-1}X^Ty\)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;For large data / many features → minimize the &lt;b&gt;cost function&lt;/b&gt; with &lt;b&gt;Gradient Descent&lt;/b&gt; ③ ④&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
