        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="regression-209" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;MSE = \(\frac{1}{m}\sum(\hat{y}-y)^2\);  the extra \(\frac{1}{2}\) only makes the derivative cleaner&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;RMSE = \(\sqrt{MSE}\) is in the same unit as y;  MAE = \(\frac{1}{m}\sum|\hat{y}-y|\) is robust to outliers&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;With L2 regularization (Ridge): \(J + \frac{\lambda}{2m}\sum_{j}\beta_j^2\)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Objective: \(\min_{\beta_0,\beta_1} J(\beta_0,\beta_1)\)  →  solved by Gradient Descent ④&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1760.0" y="720.0" width="620.0" height="105.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="regression-210" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#7030A0&quot;&gt;❓ Doing this answers:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Which slope makes the line least wrong?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#333333&quot;&gt;→ the bottom of the bowl: β₁ = 0.6 with J = 0.24; every other slope gives a larger average error&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5EEFB;strokeColor=#9673A6;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1760.0" y="835.0" width="620.0" height="54.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="regression-211" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#9673A6;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=10;fontFamily=Helvetica;endFill=1;endSize=6;dashed=1;" edge="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
