        <mxCell id="regression-394" value="✘ Funnel → heteroscedasticity" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#FF0000;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2090.0" y="1345.0" width="270.0" height="20.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="regression-395" value="&lt;b&gt;Checklist:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;L&lt;/b&gt;inearity — relationship between x and y is linear&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;I&lt;/b&gt;ndependence — residuals are not correlated (no pattern over time)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;N&lt;/b&gt;ormality — residuals \(\epsilon \sim N(0,\sigma^2)\) (see Distributions page)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;E&lt;/b&gt;qual variance (homoscedasticity) — constant spread of residuals&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Multiple regression adds: no &lt;b&gt;multicollinearity&lt;/b&gt; between features (check VIF)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sensitive to outliers → inspect with Z-score / IQR (Anomaly Detection page)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1780.0" y="1380.0" width="600.0" height="190.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="regression-396" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#7030A0&quot;&gt;❓ Doing this answers:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Can I trust the line's p-values and confidence intervals?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#333333&quot;&gt;→ only if residuals look like the left plot (random band); a funnel means unequal variance → transform y or use robust standard errors&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5EEFB;strokeColor=#9673A6;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1780.0" y="1580.0" width="600.0" height="68.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
