        <mxCell id="regression-668" value="$$CV(\alpha)=\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}MSE_k(\alpha)$$" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=14;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2000.0" y="2220.0" width="330.0" height="44.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="regression-669" value="&lt;b&gt;How to choose:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;Validation curve: pick the complexity where &lt;b&gt;validation&lt;/b&gt; error is lowest (degree 4); training error always keeps falling&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Grid of α on a &lt;b&gt;log scale&lt;/b&gt;; choose the α with min CV error, or the &lt;b&gt;1-SE rule&lt;/b&gt; (simplest model within one standard error of the min)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lasso: same procedure — larger α → more coefficients exactly 0 (feature selection); Elastic Net: grid over α × l1_ratio&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Time series: use &lt;b&gt;walk-forward / TimeSeriesSplit&lt;/b&gt; instead of shuffled K-fold; refit on all training data with the chosen value&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Final check on an untouched &lt;b&gt;test set&lt;/b&gt; — never tune on it&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1460.0" y="2300.0" width="920.0" height="125.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
