        <mxCell id="classification-176" value="&lt;b&gt;How it works:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;Step 1 — compute the linear score exactly like Linear Regression&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Step 2 — pass it through the sigmoid → probability of class 1&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Step 3 — threshold the probability → class label&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Boundary \(\beta_0+\beta_1x_1+\beta_2x_2=0\) is a straight line → add polynomial features for curves&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Multi-class: &lt;b&gt;Softmax&lt;/b&gt; \(\hat{p}_k = \frac{e^{z_k}}{\sum_j e^{z_j}}\)  (or One-vs-Rest)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Linear Regression with a 0/1 target fails: outputs outside [0,1] and outliers shift the line&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1100.0" y="635.0" width="580.0" height="145.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="classification-177" value="&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#7030A0&quot;&gt;❓ Doing this answers:&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Which class does a new point belong to?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#333333&quot;&gt;→ compute z: above the green line z &gt; 0 → p̂ &gt; 0.5 → class 1; below → class 0; on the line the model is 50/50&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F5EEFB;strokeColor=#9673A6;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1100.0" y="845.0" width="580.0" height="54.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
