        <mxCell id="kernel-1284" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Small k&lt;/b&gt; → follows noise (low bias, high variance);  &lt;b&gt;large k&lt;/b&gt; → too smooth (high bias, low variance)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Pick k with cross-validation: hold out each point (or fold), predict it from the rest, average the error&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use an odd k for binary problems to avoid ties;  a rule of thumb is \(k \approx \sqrt{n}\)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Curse of dimensionality: with many features all points look equally far → reduce dimensions first (PCA)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
