        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ensemble-588" value="&lt;b&gt;Reading the learning curve:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;Gap between the curves = variance (here 0.14 at n = 200)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Validation curve still falling → &lt;b&gt;more data will help&lt;/b&gt;; flat → more data alone won't&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Here: validation error 0.24 → 0.21 (already flat → improve features / tree depth instead)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Both curves high and close → high bias → deeper trees / better features&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1940.0" y="2160.0" width="440.0" height="105.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ensemble-589" value="&lt;table style=&quot;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:11px&quot; border=&quot;1&quot; cellpadding=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background:#EEEEEE&quot;&gt;&lt;th&gt;Hyperparameter&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Effect&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;How to choose&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;n_estimators&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;more trees → lower variance, never overfits, slower&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;increase until OOB error plateaus (panel ⑤)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;max_samples&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;smaller samples → more diverse but weaker trees&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;OOB grid (a): 50–100 % typical&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;max_features&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;fewer features per split → decorrelated trees (Random Forest)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;√p (classification), p/3 (regression), or grid&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;base-tree depth&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;deep trees = low bias, high variance (what bagging fixes)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;fully grown or tune max_depth / min_samples_leaf&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1460.0" y="2315.0" width="920.0" height="150.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ensemble-590" value="&lt;b&gt;How to choose:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;OOB error ≈ cross-validation error for free → tune bagging / Random Forest without a separate validation split&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Time series: bootstrap breaks temporal order → use block bootstrap / sequential bootstrap (López de Prado) and purged CV&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1460.0" y="2475.0" width="920.0" height="65.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ensemble-591" value="The whole ensemble family: Boosting, Voting &amp;amp; Stacking" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="400.0" y="2640.0" width="1600.0" height="35.2" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ensemble-592" value="Bagging (above) is one of four ways to combine models. Same algorithm vs different algorithms, and parallel vs sequential training, as in the original &amp;#x27;Ensemble Learning Categorization&amp;#x27;." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#555555;" vertex="1" parent="1">
