        <mxCell id="clustering-261" value="&lt;b&gt;Where:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Assign step&lt;/b&gt;: every point joins the cluster of its nearest centroid (Euclidean distance ②)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Update step&lt;/b&gt;: every centroid moves to the mean of its points (③) — dashed arrows show the move&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Repeat until no point changes cluster (or centroids move less than a tolerance) — always converges, maybe to a local minimum&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Poor start → use &lt;b&gt;k-means++&lt;/b&gt; (spread-out initial centroids) and run several times (&lt;i&gt;n_init&lt;/i&gt;), keep the lowest inertia&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="420.0" y="670.0" width="1280.0" height="105.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
