        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="timeseries-652" value="&lt;b&gt;Choosing the lag N:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;Choose N with the &lt;b&gt;PACF&lt;/b&gt; (last significant lag), information criteria (&lt;b&gt;AIC/BIC&lt;/b&gt;) or validation error&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Split train / test &lt;b&gt;by time&lt;/b&gt; (never shuffle) and fit scalers on the training part only — otherwise look-ahead leakage&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Longer N = more memory but fewer samples and more parameters; LSTM can learn longer dependencies than AR&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
