        <mxCell id="tstests-434" value="Two &lt;b&gt;independent&lt;/b&gt; random walks:&lt;br&gt;β̂ = 0.87, t = 25.2, R² = 0.72&lt;br&gt;but ADF on residuals τ = -2.18 → &lt;font color='#FF0000'&gt;&lt;b&gt;not cointegrated&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;→ the 'relationship' is meaningless" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1230.0" y="2020.0" width="240.0" height="100.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tstests-435" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;Both series must be I(1) (unit root in levels, stationary after one difference) before testing cointegration&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Johansen test&lt;/b&gt;: many series at once, finds the number of cointegrating vectors (trace / max-eigenvalue statistics)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Pairs trading: trade the spread when it is ±2σ from its mean; exit when it reverts; re-estimate β on a rolling window&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Cointegration ≠ correlation: returns can be correlated without cointegration (and vice versa)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="420.0" y="2185.0" width="1060.0" height="105.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
