        <mxCell id="featureeng-211" value="&lt;b&gt;Why it matters:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;Distance models (kNN, K-Means, SVM) &amp; PCA: large-unit features dominate otherwise&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Gradient descent: round cost contours → faster convergence&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Regularization (Ridge / Lasso) penalises all coefficients fairly&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Trees don't need scaling (splits are order-based)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=10;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
