        <mxCell id="explain-406" value="&lt;b&gt;Reading:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul style=&quot;margin:2px 0 0 0;padding-left:16px&quot;&gt;&lt;li&gt;PDP shows the &lt;b&gt;average&lt;/b&gt; effect; spread-out or crossing ICE lines reveal interactions hidden by the average&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Here RSI and RSI_copy are moved together; moving one alone would create unrealistic rows (correlation pitfall ③)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use ALE plots when features are strongly correlated; PDP assumes the varied feature is independent of the others&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;fontColor=default;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1220.0" y="1540.0" width="1160.0" height="85.0" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
